  "body": "Suppose we try to fetch keys from some homeserver we've never heard of.\r\n\r\nWe'll first try to use StoreKeyFetcher, which calls https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/9bb2eac71962970d02842bca441f4bcdbbf93a11/synapse/crypto/keyring.py#L513 to read from `server_signature_keys`: https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/b76f1a4d5f918def1f643910939b80e9e035e07f/synapse/storage/databases/main/keys.py#L65-L68\r\n\r\nThat will return no keys. So next we'll try the PerspectivesKeyFetcher, but that will do nothing because we have no trusted key server configured.\r\n\r\nSo next we try the ServerKeyFetcher. That will fetch keys via\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/9bb2eac71962970d02842bca441f4bcdbbf93a11/synapse/crypto/keyring.py#L844\r\n\r\nand https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/9bb2eac71962970d02842bca441f4bcdbbf93a11/synapse/crypto/keyring.py#L901-L905\r\n\r\nbefore caling https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/9bb2eac71962970d02842bca441f4bcdbbf93a11/synapse/crypto/keyring.py#L605\r\n\r\nwhich writes to `server_keys_json`.\r\n\r\nIf we try to re-fetch keys for that server, we'll try the StoreKeyFetcher. But as we saw above, that reads from a different table (`server_signature_keys`). So we'll end up repeating the same steps and making another federation request via ServerKeyFetcher.\r\n",
